This is a fun puzzle-platformer with really cleverly designed levels. I had always dismissed this series because for some reason, the visuals reminded me of casual mobile games... That was a huge mistake on my part. This is not a game for casual gamers in the slightest. It really makes you think hard. The difficulty reaches insane levels towards the end. I honestly don't know how anyone could even finish the game without consulting a walkthrough. Thankfully, it's not an incredibly long game. The soundtrack is pleasant and cheerful (especially
), and I found it a nice break from all the depressing violence and death I would otherwise be experiencing in other games. The ending of this game is so bizarre and messed up. But you don't play this kind of game for its story. It's a totally forgettable, ignorable aspect of the game.
The sequel to this game is probably way better, but I like to play all series in order when possible. I don't regret doing that with Toki Tori. For the ridiculously cheap price you can usually get this for during sales, it's totally worth a buy + playthrough if you like puzzle games!

